          "To eliminate this redundancy, Microsoft researchers introduced the Zero Redundancy Optimizer (ZeRO) in 2019, paving the way for training 100B+ models.",
          "ZeRO organizes memory sharding into three progressive stages: ZeRO Stage 1 (ZeRO-1), ZeRO Stage 2 (ZeRO-2), and ZeRO Stage 3 (ZeRO-3).",
          "ZeRO-1 partitions the 12 bytes of AdamW optimizer states across N GPUs; each GPU updates only 1/N of the optimizer states, yielding up to a 4x memory reduction.",
