          "To prevent this collapse, the Switch Transformer introduces an Auxiliary Load Balancing Loss: L_aux = alpha * E * sum(f_i * P_i).",
          "Here, f_i is the fraction of tokens dispatched to expert i, and P_i is the average gating probability assigned to expert i across the batch.",
          "Under uniform load balancing where f_i = 1/E and P_i = 1/E for all experts, the auxiliary loss reaches its mathematical minimum of alpha.",
          "Any deviation where an expert receives a disproportionate share of tokens increases the dot product, penalizing the loss.",
          "The hyperparameter alpha (typically set to 0.01) controls the strength of the balancing pressure relative to language modeling cross-entropy.",
          "Tuning alpha ensures that the optimizer balances expert loads without restricting the model's natural ability to specialize.",
